#X obj 659 11 dyn.expand~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 175 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A mono downward expander. Unlike a compressor \, which
reduces the level of loud signals above the threshold \, an expander
reduces the level of quiet signals below the threshold \, thereby increasing
the dynamic range of the material. Instead of the traditional "ratio"
control \, it uses a strength parameter \, which makes it easy to use
the object as a gentle expander or as a full-fledged noise gate (with
high strength values).;
#X obj 240 217 ui.link @background_color 0.90196 0.90196 0.90196
@title Dynamic range       compression @url
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_range_compression;
